    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: on berlin a STOCHASTIC 'Blue Stochastic Platoon' (TKB 305: 3 squads of 10, defending at (300,300)) and a PHYSICAL 'Red Patrol' (four men) marching from 700 m north to 150 m. Judge (CE-8307, X-5 / D-P7 'one level at a time'): (1) when the patrol enters the band the platoon hands over and becomes a physical COMMAND unit whose roster is its 3 squads - never 30 men; (2) each squad is a stochastic unit named <platoon>/<s> with the stable key uuid5(<platoon>, child:<s>), carrying exactly its 10 slots (the counts conserved); (3) the platoon's Defend order re-resolves to PlatoonDefend (it now commands squads); (4) as the patrol closes, each squad splits in turn into its men, named <platoon>/<s>/<n> with the key uuid5(<squad>, child:<n>), its roster the 10 men; (5) the platoon's own slot table keeps 30 men up. Fail: a flat split into 30 men, a squad with the wrong slots, a missing or re-keyed child. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh agg-platoon-splits-into-squads"
  },
